    "answer": {
      "short": "$8,\\ 12,\\ 24,\\ 32,\\ 40$. These are multiples of $4$.",
      "worked": "Equivalent fractions are made by multiplying both numerator and denominator by the same whole number:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{1\\times2}{4\\times2}=\\frac{2}{8}\\\\\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{1\\times3}{4\\times3}=\\frac{3}{12}\\\\\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{1\\times6}{4\\times6}=\\frac{6}{24}\\\\\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{1\\times8}{4\\times8}=\\frac{8}{32}\\\\\\frac{1}{4}&=\\frac{1\\times10}{4\\times10}=\\frac{10}{40}\\end{align*}$$\nCircle $8,12,24,32,40$: each denominator is a multiple of $4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
